config BR2_PACKAGE_ENTER
	bool "enter"
	depends on BR2_USE_MMU
	help
	  Static isolated-rootfs launcher with best-effort namespace isolation.

	  Installs /enter in the target rootfs. Copy that binary into
	  another rootfs at <rootfs>/enter and run it: the launcher
	  takes its own parent directory as the rootfs and enters it
	  with whatever isolation the running kernel permits.

	  Optional PID, UTS, and IPC namespaces are enabled when supported.
	  A mount namespace is required. Running as a non-root user requires
	  unprivileged user namespaces to be enabled by the host kernel.
	  Missing OverlayFS, devtmpfs, sysfs, and devpts support use documented
	  fallbacks or warnings where possible.

	  The rootfs directory must contain /usr and /tmp. A usable /dev and
	  mounted /proc on the host are required; setup failures are reported as errors.
